<div class="container masterplan">

<h1 id="top">Schema Master Plan — Database System Consolidation</h1>

<div class="last-updated doc-muted">
    Created: 2026-08-24 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Version: 1.1 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Status: COORDINATOR (schema branch)
</div>

<p class="mp-back-link"><a href="/Documentation/MASTER_PLAN">← Back to Master Plan</a></p>

<div class="notice">
    <strong>Scope correction (v1.1).</strong> The original framing put <em>schema-compare</em> at the center. That is
    wrong. Schema-compare is a <strong>subset</strong> of a much larger, highly fragmented database system. Across
    <code>lib/Comserv/</code> there are many components with "DB" in their name — <code>DBEncy</code>, <code>DBForager</code>,
    <code>AccountingDB</code>, <code>HybridDB</code>, <code>RemoteDB</code>, <code>Util::SchemaCompare</code>,
    <code>Util::Accounting::Migrator</code>, <code>Util::BackupManager</code>, <code>Util::DatabaseSchemaCache</code>,
    plus the <code>DBSchemaManager</code> referenced by docs — each added by separate AI improvements
    <strong>before plans were enforced</strong>. This plan now treats the <em>entire DB-access layer</em> as the thing
    to reconsider and simplify, and schema-compare as one part of it.
</div>

<p>This is the single entry point for how Comserv manages its two database engines <em>and</em> the sprawl of code that
talks to them. It does <strong>not</strong> replace the sub-plans — it sequences them, records what is done, names the
gates, and — critically — records the <strong>consolidation debt</strong> this branch must address. The schema/doc
story was spread across seven partially overlapping docs, and MASTER_PLAN references three plans that are
<strong>not yet written</strong> (see <a href="#gaps">§9 Gaps</a>).</p>

<div class="doc-info">
    <strong>Vocabulary:</strong> <strong>Result class</strong> = a <code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/.../Result/Foo.pm</code>
    file declaring a table via <code>__PACKAGE__-&gt;table(...)</code> + <code>add_columns(...)</code> — the single source of
    truth for a table's shape. <strong>Schema-compare</strong> = the in-app workflow (<code>/admin/compare_schema</code>)
    that diffs Result classes against live tables. <strong>Clone</strong> = the Maria→PG copy pipeline
    (<code>Util::Accounting::Migrator</code> + <code>/Accounting/setup</code>). <strong>DB system</strong> = the union of every
    model/util/controller that opens a database connection.
</div>

